{"id": "EUVD-2026-96344", "enisaUuid": "4e36a7b6-5ff0-3b10-b8de-af60f7b2edeb", "description": "cc-connect through 1.5.0 contains a missing authentication vulnerability in the MAX platform adapter webhook mode in platform/max/max.go that accepts unauthenticated updates when no webhook_secret is configured. Remote attackers reaching the webhook listener on port 8080 can forge updates with an allowed or admin user_id to run privileged commands like /shell on the host.", "datePublished": "2026-10-10T14:35:04", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T11:36:36", "baseScore": 9.2, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/chenhg5/cc-connect/issues/1968", "https://github.com/chenhg5/cc-connect", "https://github.com/chenhg5/cc-connect/blob/v1.5.0/platform/max/max.go#L287-L305", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/cc-connect-through-1.5.0-missing-authentication-via-max-webhook-sender-spoofing"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-108549", "GHSA-h8j8-r6g6-37hc"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.45, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "a9bd129d-386f-309d-94a0-ff0461d67029", "product": {"name": "cc-connect", "vendor": {"name": "chenhg5"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.5.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "2b83a98e-aadf-3cf5-b255-6d81d74681a1", "vendor": {"name": "chenhg5"}}], "isExploited": false}